      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That \"unraveling thread\" feeling is a powerful illusion, rooted in the belief that your worth is tied to perfection. Cutting yourself out wouldn't save the tapestry; it would only remove a part that was already woven in. Instead of viewing yourself as a flaw, see yourself as a necessary, complex part of the whole, even if that part is struggling. There is profound strength in acknowledging the damage and choosing to heal, not in erasing yourself.",
